From 6be63b777e99dbfd33ee7afd17b13b0910b40856 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tiago Rezende <tiagosr@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 21:15:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(portmidi): ALSA virtual ports stamped with
 pre-allocation seq queue never delivered (A133)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

alsa_create_virtual() stamped the port's timestamp queue with the
global `queue` variable, which is zero-initialized and only
lazy-allocated by alsa_use_queue() at the first Pm_Open. Virtual
ports created before that first open therefore carried queue 0 — a
queue owned by a different client (on the A133 it is owned by
PipeWire-RT-Event and Stopped). The ALSA sequencer schedules
tick-timestamped events on that queue, so events addressed to our
virtual input were never delivered; aconnect loopback into the
virtual input silently produced nothing.

Guard the three timestamp lines on queue_used > 0; ports created
before the shared queue exists keep the kernel default (real-time)
timestamping, which delivers correctly. Verified on-device: A133
aconnect out->in loopback into the app's own virtual ports
delivers note_on after this guard.
---
 pm_linux/pmlinuxalsa.c | 21 +++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/pm_linux/pmlinuxalsa.c b/pm_linux/pmlinuxalsa.c
index 2ad0973..376efd2 100644
--- a/pm_linux/pmlinuxalsa.c
+++ b/pm_linux/pmlinuxalsa.c
@@ -354,10 +354,23 @@ static PmError alsa_create_virtual(int is_input, const char *name,
     snd_seq_port_info_set_name(pinfo, name);
     snd_seq_port_info_set_port(pinfo, id);
     snd_seq_port_info_set_port_specified(pinfo, 1);
-    /* next 3 lines needed to generate timestamp - PaulLiu */
-    snd_seq_port_info_set_timestamping(pinfo, 1);
-    snd_seq_port_info_set_timestamp_real(pinfo, 0);
-    snd_seq_port_info_set_timestamp_queue(pinfo, queue);
+    /* next 3 lines needed to generate timestamp - PaulLiu.
+       Guarded: the shared queue is lazy-allocated by alsa_use_queue()
+       at the first Pm_Open, so at virtual-port creation time `queue`
+       is still its zero-initialized default — a queue owned by a
+       different client (on the A133 it is queue 0, owned by
+       PipeWire-RT-Event). A port stamped with a queue its client does
+       not own never receives events (the ALSA sequencer drops the
+       tick-scheduled delivery), so loopback into the virtual input
+       silently delivered nothing there. Ports created before the
+       queue exists keep the kernel default (real-time) timestamping,
+       which delivers correctly; event timestamps are ignored by
+       handle_event anyway. */
+    if (queue_used > 0) {
+        snd_seq_port_info_set_timestamping(pinfo, 1);
+        snd_seq_port_info_set_timestamp_real(pinfo, 0);
+        snd_seq_port_info_set_timestamp_queue(pinfo, queue);
+    }
 
     err = snd_seq_create_port(seq, pinfo);
     if (err < 0) {
-- 
